Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: pngrutil.c
Line: 4911
Function: png_read_reinit
Bug type: heap-buffer-overflow
CWE: CWE-122
Explanation: After updating png_ptr->width/height and recomputing png_ptr->rowbytes for the next APNG frame, the code zeroes png_ptr->prev_row with length png_ptr->rowbytes + 1 without ensuring that the previously allocated prev_row buffer is large enough for the new frame. If next_frame_width (and thus rowbytes) is larger than the allocation made for the prior frame, this memset writes past the end of the heap buffer.

